{"title":"2015 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 17","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solutions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solutions</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Solution_7_(Solution_3_but_explained_better)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 7 (Solution 3 but explained better)</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(HOW_TO_THINK_CRITICALLY!!!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (HOW TO THINK CRITICALLY!!!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Jeremy's father drives him to school in rush hour traffic in 20 minutes. One day there is no traffic, so his father can drive him 18 miles per hour faster and gets him to school in 12 minutes. How far in miles is it to school?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/a/40a02a26d28004ae85b8e25ae86a061a2de34722.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 4 \\qquad \\textbf{(B) } 6 \\qquad \\textbf{(C) } 8 \\qquad \\textbf{(D) } 9 \\qquad \\textbf{(E) } 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"362\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solutions\">Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>For starters, we identify d as distance and v as velocity (speed)\n</p><p>Writing the equation gives us: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/c/4dcce13fab37fcd84d6901dcc7135bac6b342133.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{d}{v}=\\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"49\" height=\"37\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/4/ab4328f8ba9760a6a6e9cdf60dd9d23bd787248d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{d}{v+18}=\\frac{1}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"93\" height=\"41\" />.\n</p><p>This gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/d/3fdcde90f3c5a721f9ebccc98e294784432a6b51.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d=\\frac{1}{5}v+3.6=\\frac{1}{3}v$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"148\" height=\"37\" />, which gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/3/a13d731a37fce52d2079d2ad202a9d97be76545a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v=27$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"54\" height=\"14\" />, which then gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/2/ba2828b57b346c08b0d037a23d4b4f7e9d9075b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}~9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"89\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/3/953f29a2b6ad8f2c5d0a2c619a084c4d6896600e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d = rt$\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/a/85a27760d36938411508d07d212df47cd35c5665.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d=\\frac{1}{3} \\times r = \\frac{1}{5} \\times (r + 18)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"198\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/8/6685a1fe1018498c7671d8c22d6accfe4998e1ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{r}{3} = \\frac{r}{5} + \\frac{18}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"93\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/6/ec6ff69f29fd72c4a30e931cbe2e92611c17fd5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10r = 270$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"77\" height=\"13\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/0/2b01608f16c8ca70de601325e4bfd5f01e066911.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = 27$\" width=\"51\" height=\"12\" />, plug into the first one and it's <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/f/f3fcbad0483656572e254e98e5ff0c67206313dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}~9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"55\" height=\"28\" /> miles to school.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>We set up an equation in terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> the distance and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> the speed In miles per hour. We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/f/64fa6866dea7b4f78e3bf6049b5b3162681cdfb9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d=\\left (\\dfrac{1}{3}\\right )(x)=\\left (\\dfrac{1}{5}\\right) (x+18)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"230\" height=\"43\" />, giving\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/4/d1462fd905bb7ab31d0490c0c5dd2fd85afb7028.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(5)(x)=(3)(x+18)\\]\" width=\"157\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/5/0f50aceae271dd099c5020078db14e29f9105ae7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[5x=3x+54\\]\" width=\"103\" height=\"14\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/a/83aea5404764b8ba4c4d66c2faa44946a0bebf46.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2x=54\\]\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/a/daac91f4974ad61351248574f30790c620247e94.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x=27\\]\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" />\nHence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/f/c0fa2d7159b810c28e17b098b97e459e4c5df56a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d=\\dfrac{27}{3}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}~9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"136\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Since it takes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/4/ac40ce1434cda0943c408cc185f5976212d95801.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> of the original time for him to get to school when there is no traffic, the speed must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/e/9ae6ca439f90be5b87b92cab8cfd6ea9e3f23475.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" /> of the speed in no traffic or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/4/7547747b133453d3c209cff6cfbf129aa67a6947.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> more. Letting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be the rate and we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/a/29a9e0f30e91634b5a4f265fc5f8850cc46bcba0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5}{3}x = x + 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"100\" height=\"38\" />, so we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/a/56a816a8c1063dc029e07da16e0a4270b5a48fa7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2x}{3} = 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"68\" height=\"38\" /> miles per hour. Solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/5/1051e7d41ec0b8bd688a872be17538413f4ee97b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$27$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> miles per hour. Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> minutes is a third of an hour, the distance would then be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> miles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/f/f3fcbad0483656572e254e98e5ff0c67206313dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}~9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"55\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>When driving in rush hour traffic, he drives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> minutes for one distance (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/6/e56aa7a788d20253549553ca6a3895eb7590ac5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1d$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"18\" height=\"13\" />) to the school. It means he drives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/302e99c1c7cd91a6ae371139e5142ccef5977dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> minutes for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> distances (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/2/9b26c8398882a95a9099c7b9516439dd6b467c65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3d$\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" />) to the school. When driving in no traffic hours, he drives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> minutes for one distance (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/6/e56aa7a788d20253549553ca6a3895eb7590ac5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1d$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"18\" height=\"13\" />) to the school. It means he drives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/302e99c1c7cd91a6ae371139e5142ccef5977dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> minutes for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> distances (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/7/7a7dab1b6e7f8f74319e4b848e6b0cd434c72007.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5d$\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" />) to the school. Subtracting these two situations, it gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/6/836704ba94a6baee7f7c88b196e0d385564bcedd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5d-3d = 18 = 2d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"146\" height=\"16\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/b/f9b038001f58296b6b526aa4dfb9e8a4815c92ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d=\\frac{18}{2}=9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"91\" height=\"38\" />. So the distance to the school would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/f/f3fcbad0483656572e254e98e5ff0c67206313dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}~9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"55\" height=\"28\" /> miles. \n~LarryFlora\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6\">Solution 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>(Ratios)\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/c/9bcade71af11c007418a7dec14f27f9aa4c02d91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{requires edits}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"115\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>In rush hour traffic, we can create this ratio for each distance we are going to try supposing the distance is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />&#160;: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> hours\n</p><p>In no traffic, we can do the same:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />&#160;: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> minutes\n</p><p>We want the ratio to be the distance to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/302e99c1c7cd91a6ae371139e5142ccef5977dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> minutes:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />&#160;: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> minutes = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />d&#160;: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/302e99c1c7cd91a6ae371139e5142ccef5977dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> minutes \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />&#160;: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> minutes = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />d&#160;: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/302e99c1c7cd91a6ae371139e5142ccef5977dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> minutes\n</p><p>This shows the speed in miles per hour. This means that the speed in the 2nd ratio has to be 18 faster than the first ratio. We get\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/6/bb62e2f839595fbde3853409e1c91b8d193fd981.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3d+18 = 5d \\cdot d=9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"160\" height=\"16\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/f/f3fcbad0483656572e254e98e5ff0c67206313dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}~9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"55\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Solution_7_.28Solution_3_but_explained_better.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_7_(Solution_3_but_explained_better)\">Solution 7 (Solution 3 but explained better)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 7 (Solution 3 but explained better)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Distance equals speed multiplied by time. Let x/60 represent the speed when Jeremy's father is driving through traffic. Let (x+18)/60 represent the speed when there is no traffic. Because distance equals speed multiplied by time, 20x/60 would represent the distance to school. The \"20\" in this expression represents the 20 minutes it takes Jeremy's father to drive to school through the traffic, and \"60\" means 60 minutes. Anyway, 20x/60 simplifies to x/3. Using the same distance equation, the expression 12(x+18)/60 also represents the distance to school. (x+18)/60 represents the speed when there is no traffic, and the \"12\" means 12 minutes it takes to get to school when there is no traffic. 12(x+18)/60 simplifies to (x+18)/5. Now, since both expressions equate to the distance to school, you get the equation x/3=(x+18)/5. Solving for x gives you 27. This means that Jeremy's father drives 27 miles per hour in traffic. To find the distance to school, simply take 27 and plug it into the expressions (x+18)/5 or x/3. Both give you 9, which is the distance to school.~Evžen D.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28HOW_TO_THINK_CRITICALLY.21.21.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(HOW_TO_THINK_CRITICALLY!!!)\">Video Solution (HOW TO THINK CRITICALLY!!!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (HOW TO THINK CRITICALLY!!!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/J15jiF1mwdU\">https://youtu.be/J15jiF1mwdU</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/rQUwNC0gqdg?t=3033\">https://youtu.be/rQUwNC0gqdg?t=3033</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TFm1jNgB4QM\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TFm1jNgB4QM</a>   ~David\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/4wZ4ToIyrnw\">https://youtu.be/4wZ4ToIyrnw</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8\" title=\"2015 AMC 8\">2015 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"2015 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Answer_Key\" title=\"2015 AMC 8 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=2015\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2015 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 16\">Problem 16</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/